comments[9]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T17:28:00.718Z",maintainer-agent,"Territory update 2026-07-13 (PR#545): the output-truth slice shipped — pm update changed_fields is now derived from the persisted before/after document diff and true no-op writes are suppressed (pm-45mb closed; JSON and TOON now agree). What srns still owns is the UNIFORM envelope grammar itself: one format-flag spelling + one envelope spec across every command, alias-preserving. Input-side MCP shape parity (pm_copy flat camelCase) also landed via pm-hno5 using the derive-from-flag-contracts pattern — that pattern (schemas generated from *_FLAG_CONTRACTS, never hand-declared) is the recommended mechanism for srns's envelope convergence too."
  "2026-08-04T08:45:28.306Z","harness:codex","GitHub report reconciliation 2026-08-04: issue #888 is canonical evidence for this existing uniform output-contract scope. External package authors guessed a wrapped create result, silently received undefined IDs, skipped closure/comment sync, and imported terminal records as open. The execution plan must publish typed flat mutation receipts versus wrapped query entities in CLI help, SDK types, contracts, scripting docs, package examples, and real-boundary fixtures. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/888"
  "2026-08-04T19:54:38.051Z","harness:codex","Implementation tranche evidence 2026-08-04: added the public SDK output-envelope registry and safe mutation-receipt parser; paired every active runtime command with an envelope contract; documented flat mutation versus wrapped read shapes in global help, scripting guidance, SDK docs, and an executable package-consumer example; typed workspace snapshot grammar failures as usage, not-found, or conflict errors. Linked envelope/snapshot tests passed 9/9. Direct repository coverage passed 433 files and 6,850 tests at 100/100/100/100. Packed-artifact npm/npx and Bun/bunx consumers both initialized trackers and parsed real create receipts. This is a cohesive advancement, while alias-preserving one-flag grammar across every legacy command remains open."
  "2026-08-04T20:56:34.004Z","harness:codex","Review evidence: corrected command-output contracts so start-task/pause-task/close-task/focus are single mutation receipts; close-many/update-many are explicit rows collections; declared lookups retain normalized full subcommand paths; parseMutationReceipt now exposes string and decoded-value overloads. Updated scripting documentation and regression tests."
  "2026-08-04T20:56:35.602Z","harness:codex","Manual isolated consumer evidence: packed @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.4 into /tmp/pm-sdk-review-offline-5BLZQZ, installed from the exact tarball in unrelated npm and Bun roots using offline caches, initialized real trackers, and parsed successful flat create receipts through npx (manual-nb4u/open) and bunx (bunmanual-zzqw/open)."
  "2026-08-21T21:17:04.297Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-21: make the universal output envelope distinguish caller-supplied legacy aliases from command-local flags synthesized to execute canonical projection modes, preserving behavior and strict migration evidence across CLI, SDK, and MCP."
  "2026-08-21T21:28:32.728Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: the expanded focused matrix initially failed for canonical include modes because synthesized command-local flags were reported as caller-supplied legacy aliases. After preserving exact raw CLI provenance through Commander reconstruction, all 12 tests pass, covering 22 declared replacements plus canonical-only, legacy-only, and mixed invocation receipts."
  "2026-08-21T22:07:13.485Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence (2026-08-22): added invocation-aware read-output receipts across SDK normalization and Commander CLI reconstruction. Canonical-only input now reports canonical_options_used without a legacy migration hint; legacy-only reports only the supplied compatibility alias; mixed input reports both surfaces deterministically. Focused read-output matrix: 54 tests passed. Full test suite: 551 files / 7706 tests passed. Coverage gate: statements 56274/56274, branches 42030/42030, functions 11705/11705, lines 54264/54264 (100% all dimensions). pnpm lint and full static assurance passed, including 167/167 runtime command grammar and 2831/2831 flag invocation parity. pnpm typecheck, contracts check, SDK surface check, changelog check, security scan, pnpm audit, and git diff check passed. Manual isolated temp-workspace acceptance passed for canonical-only, legacy-only, and mixed CLI invocations; the temporary root was removed after verification. GitHub open alerts: Dependabot 0, code scanning 0, secret scanning 0. Dependency inventory found only out-of-range major upgrades npm-package-arg 13 to 14 and TypeScript 6 to 7; no in-range or security update is pending in this scoped change."
  "2026-08-21T22:23:27.186Z","harness:codex","PR #1081 review evidence: DeepScan reported one valid low-impact UNUSED_PARAM finding at src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts. Removed the stale requested parameter and its single call argument. Focused regression passed 14/14 and full TypeScript checks passed. ESLint, duplicate detection, repository static assurance, contract/parity gates, graph composition, record integrity, and diff checks passed. The first aggregate lint run observed a transient local next-command transport sample of 525ms over the 440ms ceiling; an immediate isolated rerun of the exact transport-floor gate passed all 6 operations, consistent with the hosted CodSpeed and CI performance checks being green."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T16:23:33.766Z",maintainer-agent,"Scope addition (pm-mpbb ledger lever c, promoted 2026-07-11 when the a22j baseline gate opened): the uniform output contract this item owns must ALSO specify a semantic exit-code contract (documented, uniform across commands, machine-checkable) - today create/update failures hide under pipes (exit codes invisible under `| tail`, see the shell-safety trap class this item already owns). One spec covers both the envelope shape and the exit-code semantics; the pm-0z7n alias deprecation fields (ledger lever b) also land in this spec."
  "2026-07-25T06:21:59.962Z","harness:claude-code","Token-efficiency doctrine, drafted 2026-07-25 to give the individual output items one ordered account of where agent tokens actually go and which lever addresses each. Measured baseline for orientation: the MCP tool surface alone costs roughly 8.2k tokens cold (28 tools, 32,979 bytes), and JSON costs 48-53 percent more than TOON for the same payload.\n\nThe levers, ordered by measured or expected saving per unit of implementation cost:\n\n1. Do not send what the caller already has. The largest remaining waste is repeat orientation: an agent re-reads a workspace that has not changed. Owned by the delta read projection filed as pm-tuadp2; an unchanged workspace should cost a header and a count, not a projection.\n2. Do not send what the caller did not ask for. Lean output shipped (null/empty omission, lean mutation echo, tag folding, counts-only validate, omitted-note counts). The remaining gap is that omission is per-command rather than contract-declared, which is exactly what pm-srns's single envelope spec fixes.\n3. Send a ceiling, not a hope. Contract-declared per-command budgets with a deterministic degradation ladder, owned by pm-5t33or. Unbounded output is the failure mode that turns one bad call into a lost context window.\n4. Send structure once. TOON's header-once tabular form already does this for rows; the same principle is unexploited for nested facets, where each item repeats its facet keys. A facet-table projection is the natural extension and belongs to the same envelope spec.\n5. Do not make the caller ask twice. Round trips cost more than payload: an envelope that omits a count forces a second call, a blocked summary without blocker ids forces a second call, an error without the valid domain forces a retry. Several tracked issues are instances of this one principle, and the envelope spec should state it as a rule: every response either answers the obvious follow-up or names the exact call that will.\n6. Move stable context out of the tool channel entirely. MCP resources and prompts, filed as pm-yf07b7, let the host carry orientation without a model-initiated call and without growing the tool count that costs roughly 500 cold-start tokens per tool.\n7. Charge the session, not the call. Per-call budgets misallocate across a session; catalog entry (27) on pm-4k6b proposes the allocation policy that makes early orientation expensive and repeat orientation nearly free.\n\nAnti-lever, recorded so it is not proposed again: shortening field names to save bytes. The measured saving is small against TOON's header-once form, and it costs the scripting contract its stable machine-readable names, which pm-psy1 guarantees and which every jq pipeline in the ecosystem depends on. Compress structure and redundancy, never identifiers.\n\nMeasurement discipline: every lever above must be argued against pm-8pnj (tokens per completed task) rather than against payload bytes in isolation, because levers 5 and 7 trade payload for round trips and only the task-level number captures that correctly."
